"<p>When you need a multi-container stack that is not in the marketplace, use the <strong>Custom compose</strong> template (<code>source.type = \"inline\"</code>).</p>\n<h2>How Custom Compose Works</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Apps → New App → Custom compose</strong>.</li>\n<li>Paste your <code>docker-compose.yml</code> content and optional <code>.env</code> variables (stored encrypted in <code>apps.custom_spec_encrypted</code>).</li>\n<li>Choose which service(s) and container port(s) Traefik should route to, and select the named volumes you want included in backups.</li>\n<li>The deploy wizard analyses your compose file in real time and validates it against Nitrobase's <strong>Compose Security Policy</strong> before deploying.</li>\n<li>After deployment, you can edit your compose file anytime under <strong>App → Settings</strong> with a diff preview and choose <strong>Save</strong> or <strong>Save and redeploy</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Routing &#x26; Safety Rules</h2>\n<p>Custom compose apps go through the exact same rewrite and security pipeline as marketplace templates (with <code>[security]</code> allowlists empty):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Traefik routing:</strong> Nitrobase strips any <code>traefik.*</code> or <code>com.docker.*</code> labels and generates a clean dynamic route file under <code>/etc/nitrobase/traefik/dynamic/app-&#x3C;key>.yml</code>. Routed containers are attached to <code>nitrobase-network</code> by container name only after <code>docker compose up</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Published ports:</strong> Any <code>ports:</code> entries in your compose file are automatically stripped; HTTP/HTTPS traffic flows through Traefik.</li>\n<li><strong>Restart policy:</strong> Services without an explicit <code>restart:</code> policy receive <code>APP_DEFAULT_RESTART</code> (<code>unless-stopped</code> by default) so they recover after a host reboot (while <code>restart: always</code> is normalized to <code>unless-stopped</code> so manual Stop persists).</li>\n<li><strong>Bind mounts:</strong> Relative paths must stay inside the app folder (<code>/etc/nitrobase/apps/&#x3C;folder></code>). If your compose mounts config files that your app creates itself at runtime, list them under <strong>Files the app creates itself</strong> (<code>dataBinds</code>) in the wizard so Nitrobase does not treat an empty directory created by Docker as a missing file error.</li>\n<li><strong>Backups:</strong> Scheduled and manual backups stop the app briefly and archive all selected named volumes into encrypted <code>.tar.zst</code> bundles.</li>\n</ul>"